    "result_text": "All green. Build succeeds and both acceptance tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the owner identity key to **v2** and reworked duplicate detection around it. Changes:\n\n**`OwnerIdentity.java`** (single source of truth)\n- `key(telephone, email, lastName)` now returns `SHA-256 hex (lower-case, 64 chars)` over `canonicalTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)`. Replaced the old plaintext `telephone|email|householdId` key.\n- Added `sha256HexLower(...)` (full 64-char lowercase hex) and a correct American **Soundex** implementation (`soundex`, with the H/W transparency and vowel-reset rules, matching the Apache Commons reference).\n- Kept `householdIdOf`/`deriveHouseholdId` as descriptive metadata only \u2014 postcode no longer feeds the key.\n\n**`EnsureIdentityUnique.java`** (the 409 check)\n- Keys both sides on the new `key(telephone, email, lastName)`. Still skips soft-deleted owners and is still preceded in the pipeline by the email-domain blocklist (`ValidateOwnerFields` \u2192 `EnsureIdentityUnique`). Two owners with the same lastName+postcode but different telephones now differ in key \u21d2 no 409 (they become a soft match). There is no separate householdId-based 409.\n\n**`FlagPossibleDuplicate.java`** (the soft match)\n- Now flags a possible duplicate when the identityKey **differs** but `soundex(lastName)` **and** postcode match \u2014 replacing the old \"normalized lastName + postcode + different telephone\" rule.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 `identityKey(owner)` computes the v2 key from `lastName`.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `identityKey` description/example to the SHA-256/soundex form.\n\nTest result: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex` (64-hex shape) and `coreRejectsDuplicateIdentity` (identical identity \u21d2 409) both pass. `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the repo.",
